Mark XXVI: app injection (local API + overlay + plugin scaffolds)

UMBRA becomes usable from within other applications.

- api.py: jarvis serve --api starts a loopback-only, token-authenticated
  JSON API (127.0.0.1 hard-bound; the LAN Bridge stays a separate PRO
  command). Endpoints: GET /health, GET /tools (tier-gated registry),
  POST /chat (synchronous full agent turn; 409 when busy). Token lives
  in <config>/api-token (0600 POSIX), rotatable via jarvis api token
  rotate (shown once) / show (masked). LITE tier: same trust envelope
  as the dashboard (loopback + token). Confirmation-gated tools are
  auto-DENIED over the API - the model points the user at the dashboard
  or Bridge for interactive approvals. Nothing is logged, least of all
  the token. API turns are logged to the conversation store (parity).
- overlay.py: jarvis overlay opens an always-on-top Tkinter companion
  (status + query box + last reply) talking to the local API.
  --attach <process> best-effort finds the process (psutil) and tags
  sent messages with a context line - the overlay observes nothing by
  itself. --clickthrough is display-only on Windows. Degrades to a
  console companion without Tkinter; --no-ui runs headless (status
  once, clean exit 0) for tests and scripting.
- plugins.py: jarvis plugin scaffold vscode|browser --out <dir> writes
  minimal starters that call the API (VS Code command + settings; MV3
  manifest + service worker + popup). No auto-install, no store
  publishing, no token embedded in generated files - tokens are
  configured at runtime through each host's own storage.
- Tests: API auth (missing/invalid/valid/rotated tokens), loopback bind
  assertion, tier gating over /tools, chat round-trip, 409 busy,
  overlay no-ui offline + online paths, scaffold file/manifest schema
  and secret-free assertions.
- Version 3.13.0.
